From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:35:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gameflex 0069: a transfer is ordered with the commands around
 it

Clair Obscur lost the device after two or three minutes with gameflex 0061
(a compute ring timeout, the GPU recovered by the kernel), with 0061 alone
as with everything after, never with the Kyty before it. Bisected on the
bench: ordering every dispatch with the writes before it changes nothing;
ordering every transfer with the commands around it keeps the game running
(13.2 images/s over 330 s, against 11.5 before 0061).

The game fills counters by DMA 6 500 times a second and reads them from its
shaders with no wait the command processor decodes, and the console gets
away with it. So transfers are the exception to following the game: a
transfer waits for the shader writes before it, two transfers over the same
bytes stay ordered, and the command after a transfer waits for it, until the
packet the game relies on is found. Astro Bot's garden keeps its pace: the
transfers of a run are few beside its draws.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/guestSync.cpp |  7 ++++++-
 src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/guestSync.h   | 15 +++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/guestSync.cpp b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/guestSync.cpp
index 4c8171b5..0450fc29 100644
--- a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/guestSync.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/guestSync.cpp
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ void GuestSync::Wrote(vk::PipelineStageFlags2 stages, vk::AccessFlags2 access) {
 void GuestSync::WroteTransfer(vk::Buffer buffer, uint64_t offset, uint64_t size) {
 	Wrote(vk::PipelineStageFlagBits2::eAllTransfer, vk::AccessFlagBits2::eTransferWrite);
 	m_transfers.push_back({buffer, offset, size});
+	m_wait = true; // the command after a transfer waits for it (see BeforeTransfer)
 }
 
 bool GuestSync::TransferOverlaps(vk::Buffer buffer, uint64_t offset, uint64_t size) const noexcept {
@@ -61,7 +62,11 @@ void GuestSync::PostDue(vk::CommandBuffer command) {
 
 void GuestSync::BeforeTransfer(vk::CommandBuffer command, vk::Buffer buffer, uint64_t offset,
                                uint64_t size) {
-	if (Due()) {
+	// Shaders wrote since the last barrier: a transfer waits for them. Transfers alone: ordered below, only
+	// over the same bytes.
+	const bool transfers_only =
+	    (m_stages & ~vk::PipelineStageFlags2 {vk::PipelineStageFlagBits2::eAllTransfer}) == vk::PipelineStageFlags2 {};
+	if (Due() || (static_cast<bool>(m_stages) && !transfers_only)) {
 		Post(command);
 		return;
 	}
diff --git a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/guestSync.h b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/guestSync.h
index 681af507..7362c7d1 100644
--- a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/guestSync.h
+++ b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/guestSync.h
@@ -28,8 +28,8 @@ public:
 	void Wait(vk::PipelineStageFlags2 stages, vk::AccessFlags2 access = {});
 	// A command wrote memory through `stages`: the next barrier releases it.
 	void Wrote(vk::PipelineStageFlags2 stages, vk::AccessFlags2 access);
-	// A transfer wrote `size` bytes of `buffer` at `offset`: the next barrier releases it, and a later transfer
-	// over the same bytes follows it, as the console's DMA engine runs its queue in order.
+	// A transfer wrote `size` bytes of `buffer` at `offset`: the command after it releases it, and a later
+	// transfer over the same bytes follows it, as the console's DMA engine runs its queue in order.
 	void WroteTransfer(vk::Buffer buffer, uint64_t offset, uint64_t size);
 	// Whether the game asked for a wait since the last barrier: one is due before the next command.
 	[[nodiscard]] bool Due() const noexcept { return m_wait && static_cast<bool>(m_stages); }
@@ -37,8 +37,15 @@ public:
 	void Post(vk::CommandBuffer command);
 	// Posts the barrier due, if one is. Outside a render pass.
 	void PostDue(vk::CommandBuffer command);
-	// Before a transfer over `size` bytes of `buffer` at `offset`: the barrier due, or, when a transfer of the
-	// run wrote those bytes, a barrier between the two transfers.
+	// Before a transfer over `size` bytes of `buffer` at `offset`: the barrier for whatever the run wrote, or,
+	// when only transfers wrote and one of them those bytes, a barrier between the two transfers.
+	//
+	// Transfers are the exception to following the game. Clair Obscur fills counters by DMA 6 500 times a
+	// second and reads them from its shaders with no wait the command processor decodes, and the console gets
+	// away with it; left unordered here, the GPU hung on a compute ring after two or three minutes, every
+	// time, and never once with every transfer ordered with the commands around it. So a transfer waits for
+	// the writes before it and the command after it waits for the transfer, until the packet the game relies
+	// on is found.
 	void BeforeTransfer(vk::CommandBuffer command, vk::Buffer buffer, uint64_t offset, uint64_t size);
 
 	// Sync1 stage flags as sync2 flags: the bits coincide.
